---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import { getWebPageSchema, getBreadcrumbSchema } from '@/utils/seo'

const schemas = [
  getWebPageSchema('Updates', 'Rate changes, new calculators and improvements to Calks.uk. Stay up to date with our latest updates.', '/updates/', '2026-10-01'),
  getBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Updates', url: '/updates/' },
  ]),
]
---

<Layout title="Updates" description="Rate changes, new calculators and improvements to Calks.uk. Stay up to date with our latest updates." schemas={schemas}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Updates</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Updates</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">Rate changes, new calculators and site improvements</p>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <!-- October 2026 — Ofgem price cap 1 Oct–31 Dec 2026 + electricity VAT cut + revised TDCV -->
      <article class="relative pl-8 border-l-2 border-primary/20">
        <div class="absolute -left-2 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
            October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Energy calculators moved to the October 2026 price cap</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">New Ofgem cap from 1 October to 31 December 2026.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/energy-bill-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">energy bill calculator</a> and nine related tools now use electricity at <strong class="text-foreground">26.32p per kWh plus 54.83p a day</strong> and gas at <strong class="text-foreground">7.97p per kWh plus 29.68p a day</strong>, Direct Debit averages for Great Britain. A typical household pays £1,723 a year, 4% more than in the summer quarter.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">No VAT on electricity until 31 March 2027.</strong> The government has removed the 5% VAT from household electricity for six months. The cap already reflects it, so nothing is added on top; gas still carries 5% VAT.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Typical usage now matches Ofgem.</strong> Ofgem cut its typical household figures in July to <strong class="text-foreground">2,500 kWh of electricity and 9,500 kWh of gas</strong> a year. Our calculators still started from the older 2,700 and 11,500, which overstated the typical bill by about £210.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Worked examples recalculated.</strong> Several examples no longer added up. The <a href="/calculator/standing-charge-savings-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">standing charge example</a> claimed a £239 saving from a zero standing charge tariff that actually saves £78, and the <a href="/calculator/underfloor-heating-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">underfloor heating example</a> put the extra cost of electric heating over gas at £273 a year when it is about £943.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- September 2026 — calkcheck round 5 (27 Sep) -->
      <article class="relative pl-8 border-l-2 border-primary/20">
        <div class="absolute -left-2 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
            September 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Apprenticeship levy, student loans, speeding fines and FSCS cover corrected</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Apprenticeship levy: no 10% top-up since 1 August 2026.</strong> Under the Growth and Skills Levy reforms the government stopped adding 10% to levy funds, and new funds now expire after 12 months instead of 24. The <a href="/calculator/apprenticeship-levy-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">apprenticeship levy calculator</a> still added the top-up. Training for apprentices aged 16 to 24 is now fully funded at any employer.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Student loans, speeding fines and the non-dom regime.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/student-loan-repayment-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">student loan repayment calculator</a> charged 9% on each plan separately; with more than one undergraduate plan you repay 9% once, over the lowest threshold (£729 a year on £35,000 with Plans 1 and 2, not £1,234). The <a href="/calculator/speed-fine-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">speeding fine calculator</a> now uses the Sentencing Council bands for each speed limit and the starting point of each band: 40 mph in a 30 is Band A, a fine of half a week&rsquo;s take-home pay. The <a href="/calculator/non-dom-tax-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">non-dom calculator</a> kept the Personal Allowance while claiming the 4-year foreign income regime, which costs you the allowance; it now shows whether claiming is worth it.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Savings: FSCS cover is £120,000.</strong> Deposit protection rose from £85,000 to <strong class="text-foreground">£120,000</strong> per person per bank on 1 December 2025. Our <a href="/calculator/ns-i-savings-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">NS&amp;I savings</a> page still quoted the old limit, and three pages still gave the Premium Bonds prize rate as 3.80% (it is 4.35%). The <a href="/calculator/offset-mortgage-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">offset mortgage calculator</a> counted the savings themselves as &ldquo;interest saved&rdquo;, showing £50,025 instead of £20,025.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Pay, leave and benefits.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/holiday-entitlement-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">holiday entitlement calculator</a> gave full-time workers 28 days whatever days they worked (4 days a week is 22.4). <a href="/calculator/shared-parental-pay-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Shared Parental Pay</a> was not capped at 37 paid weeks, and <a href="/calculator/paternity-pay-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">paternity pay</a> now reflects the day-one right to paternity leave from 6 April 2026. <a href="/calculator/pension-credit-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Pension Credit</a> rounds savings income up, as the rules require, and the <a href="/calculator/childcare-cost-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">childcare cost calculator</a> asks how many hours you pay for.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Mortgages and pensions.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/buy-to-let-mortgage-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">buy-to-let mortgage calculator</a> now tests the rent at the regulator&rsquo;s stress rate (pay rate plus 2 points, at least 5.5%, unless fixed for 5 years or more), and the <a href="/calculator/salary-sacrifice-pension-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">salary sacrifice pension calculator</a> shows the tax relief on relief-at-source contributions it had left at zero.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- September 2026 — calkcheck round 4 (27 Sep) -->
      <article class="relative pl-8 border-l-2 border-primary/20">
        <div class="absolute -left-2 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
            September 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Scottish tax above £100,000, pension relief and fuel prices corrected</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Scottish income tax above £100,000 corrected.</strong> Scottish bands apply to income after the Personal Allowance, so when the allowance tapers above £100,000 every Scottish threshold moves down with it. The <a href="/calculator/scottish-income-tax-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Scottish income tax</a>, <a href="/calculator/take-home-pay-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">take-home pay</a> and <a href="/calculator/tax-year-comparison-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">tax year comparison</a> calculators kept the thresholds fixed and under-taxed Scottish earners above £100,000: on £150,000 the tax is <strong class="text-foreground">£59,634.35</strong>, not £56,366.15. Figures below £100,000 are unchanged.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Thresholds are frozen until April 2031.</strong> Budget 2025 extended the freeze on the Personal Allowance, the higher-rate threshold and the National Insurance thresholds by three years. Our tax year comparison still said the freeze ended in 2028.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Pension tax relief, shared parental leave and NHS pay.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/pension-tax-relief-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">pension tax relief calculator</a> missed the Personal Allowance restored in the £100,000 to £125,140 band (relief of £15,084 on a £25,140 contribution, 60%) and gave 40% instead of 45% at the top rate; it now also handles Scotland. The <a href="/calculator/shared-parental-leave-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">shared parental leave calculator</a> counted the two compulsory weeks twice. The <a href="/calculator/nhs-pay-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">NHS pay calculator</a> now deducts NHS Pension contributions, uses the real 2026/27 pay points and adds London weighting (HCAS).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Fuel prices updated.</strong> Six motoring calculators, including <a href="/calculator/fuel-cost-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">fuel cost</a> and <a href="/calculator/mpg-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">MPG</a>, assumed petrol at 135p a litre. The government&rsquo;s weekly average for the week of 21 September 2026 was <strong class="text-foreground">172p</strong> (diesel 196p), so every cost per mile was about a fifth too low.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Child Benefit charge, Marriage Allowance and overdrafts.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/high-income-child-benefit-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">High Income Child Benefit Charge</a> page said the charge moved to household income in April 2026; that plan was dropped and it is still based on your own income, and you can now pay it through your tax code. The <a href="/calculator/marriage-allowance-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Marriage Allowance</a> page wrongly excluded Scottish intermediate-rate taxpayers, who do qualify. The <a href="/calculator/overdraft-cost-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">overdraft calculator</a> treated the EAR as a simple rate, overstating the cost of a short overdraft by about 17%.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Contractors, landlords and heating.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/ir35-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">IR35 calculator</a> stopped taxing the director&rsquo;s salary once income passed £100,000, and the page overstated the gap between working inside and outside IR35. The <a href="/calculator/heat-pump-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">heat pump calculator</a> now takes your heating oil price and deducts the Boiler Upgrade Scheme grant (£9,000 when replacing oil or LPG until March 2027).</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- September 2026 — calkcheck round 3 (27 Sep) -->
      <article class="relative pl-8 border-l-2 border-primary/20">
        <div class="absolute -left-2 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
            September 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Salary sacrifice, bonus, dividend and care calculators corrected</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Salary sacrifice NI from April 2029 is now law, with a £2,000 allowance.</strong> The National Insurance Contributions (Employer Pensions Contributions) Act 2026 received Royal Assent on 29 April. The first £2,000 a year you sacrifice into a pension stays free of NI; above that, both you and your employer pay NI. Our <a href="/calculator/ni-salary-sacrifice-2029-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">salary sacrifice 2029 calculator</a> removed the whole NI saving, so on a £50,000 salary with £5,000 sacrificed it showed a £400 loss. The real figure is <strong class="text-foreground">£240</strong>, and it now shows the employer&rsquo;s extra NI too.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Bonus NI and dividend tax corrected.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/bonus-tax-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">bonus tax calculator</a> worked out NI over the whole year, but employees pay NI pay period by pay period, so a £5,000 bonus on a £35,000 salary loses £176 in NI, not £400. Directors can switch to the annual method. The <a href="/calculator/dividend-tax-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">dividend tax calculator</a> now lets unused Personal Allowance cover dividends (£20,000 of dividends with no other income is taxed £744.98, not £2,096.25) and applies the taper above £100,000.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Inheritance tax and probate.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/inheritance-tax-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">inheritance tax calculator</a> tapered the residence nil-rate band after the spouse exemption; the law tests the whole estate first, and the band is capped at the value of the home left to children, which you can now enter. The <a href="/calculator/probate-fee-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">probate fee calculator</a> charged £16 for every copy of the grant; copies ordered with the application have cost <strong class="text-foreground">£2</strong> since 6 July 2026.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Care costs, employer costs and visa fees.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/care-cost-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">care cost calculator</a> now uses 2026 care-home fees, lets residents keep the £31.80 Personal Expenses Allowance and protects the £241.45 Minimum Income Guarantee for care at home. The <a href="/calculator/employer-cost-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">employer cost calculator</a> charged pension on the whole salary instead of qualifying earnings (£862.80, not £1,050, on £35,000). The <a href="/calculator/visa-fee-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">visa fee calculator</a> page now quotes the April 2026 fees throughout, charges children the £776 health surcharge, adds the £130 citizenship ceremony and shows the Graduate visa at 2 years (18 months for applications from 1 January 2027).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Car import, car insurance and VAT registration.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/car-import-duty-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">car import duty calculator</a> page still described non-EU duty at the motor caravan rate; passenger cars pay <strong class="text-foreground">10%</strong>, individual vehicle approval costs £199 and cars over 10 years old are exempt. The <a href="/calculator/car-insurance-estimate-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">car insurance estimator</a> took a no-claims discount off prices that already included one, so it showed about £160 a year; it is now calibrated to the ABI average of £566. The <a href="/calculator/vat-threshold-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">VAT threshold calculator</a> said a steady £6,000 a month would cross £90,000 in three months; at that rate it never does.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Credit cards and mortgages.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/credit-card-repayment-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">credit card repayment calculator</a> treated APR as a simple annual rate, overstating interest; it now converts it properly and compares paying the minimum. The <a href="/calculator/mortgage-affordability-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">mortgage affordability calculator</a> caps borrowing at 95% loan-to-value, takes off existing credit commitments and shows the monthly payment at the current average two-year fix of 5.73%. Pages that still described the Bank of England&rsquo;s fixed stress test, withdrawn in 2022, now say lenders set their own.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- September 2026 — browser QA corrections (26 Sep) -->
      <article class="relative pl-8 border-l-2 border-primary/20">
        <div class="absolute -left-2 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
            September 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">State Pension age, spouse visa and redundancy calculators corrected</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Corrected: State Pension age for people born in 1960 and early 1961.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/state-pension-age-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">State Pension age calculator</a> gave everyone born in 1960 an age of 67. Anyone born before 6 April 1960 reaches it at <strong class="text-foreground">66</strong>, and those born 6 April 1960 to 5 March 1961 at 66 plus 1 to 11 months, so some people were shown months still to wait for a pension they can already claim. It now follows the tables in the Pensions Act.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Corrected: whose income counts for a spouse visa.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/spouse-visa-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">spouse visa calculator</a> added the applicant&rsquo;s own earnings to the £29,000 test. For a first visa from outside the UK only your UK partner&rsquo;s earnings count; the calculator now asks which route you are on and works out the savings you would need in total.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Redundancy weeks and short service fixed.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/redundancy-pay-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">redundancy pay</a>, <a href="/calculator/settlement-agreement-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">settlement agreement</a> and <a href="/calculator/employment-tribunal-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">employment tribunal</a> calculators counted a year at the higher rate half a year early, and paid redundancy with under 2 years&rsquo; service. The settlement calculator no longer adds an assumed ex-gratia payment of half your salary; you enter what you have been offered, and it now includes NI on notice and holiday pay.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Electric cars get the Congestion Charge discount.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/ulez-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">ULEZ calculator</a> charged electric cars the full £18; with Auto Pay they pay <strong class="text-foreground">£13.50</strong>. TfL penalties are now shown at £180 (£90 if paid within 14 days), and the closed London scrappage scheme is no longer presented as open.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Childcare savings no longer overstated.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/childcare-entitlement-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">30 hours childcare calculator</a> assumed your weekly fee bought exactly 30 hours. It now asks how many hours you use, so a full-time place shows the funded hours covering 30 of them.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- September 2026 — calkcheck round 2 (26 Sep) -->
      <article class="relative pl-8 border-l-2 border-primary/20">
        <div class="absolute -left-2 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="mb-2">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
            September 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Mortgage rates, Winter Fuel Payment for couples, and inheritance tax on pensions</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Mortgage rates brought up to date.</strong> Our mortgage pages still described two-year fixes at 3.8% to 4.5%. Fixed rates rose again through 2026 as swap rates climbed, and Moneyfacts put the average two-year fix at <strong class="text-foreground">5.73%</strong> and the average SVR at 7.13% in mid-September. The <a href="/calculator/remortgage-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">remortgage calculator</a> now judges a switch over the length of the new deal rather than the whole term.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Winter Fuel Payment for couples of different ages.</strong> Where one partner is 80 or over and the other is not, the older partner gets <strong class="text-foreground">£200</strong> and the younger £100; the <a href="/calculator/winter-fuel-payment-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Winter Fuel Payment calculator</a> was showing £150. The opt-out for this winter has closed, and HMRC starts recovering payments from people over £35,000 through tax codes in January 2027.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong class="text-foreground">Inheritance tax on pensions is now law.</strong> The <a href="/calculator/inheritance-tax-pension-calculator/" class="text-primary hover:underline">pension IHT calculator</a> described the April 2027 change as a proposal and said the pension scheme pays. Under the Finance Act 2026 the personal representatives are liable, and the calculator now removes the residence nil-rate band above £2 million, which on a £1.9m estate with a £400k pension adds <strong class="text-foreground">£60,000</strong> of tax.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500 shrink-0"></span>
